        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Targeted synthesis: 17 mL of 1 M PhNH2 in THF is treated with 17 mL of 1 M NaN(SiMe3)2 in THF and stirred 1 h. (Me2SiO)3 (0.34 g, 1.55 mmol) is added; after a further hour GdBr3 (1.25 g, 3.1 mmol) is added to the orange solution. After two days the solution is filtered from the precipitate and layered with an equal volume of n-heptane, giving crystals of 3 in a few days. An unplanned route (0.69 g GdBr3, 1.74 mmol; 5.21 mL 1 M PhNH2 in THF; 5.21 mL 1 M NaN(SiMe3)2 in THF; 10 mL THF; 3 d at 20 °C; n-heptane layering) also gave orange-yellow blocks of 3 in two weeks (0.4 g, 0.16 mmol, 8.9%). The oxasilylamido ligand is attributed to reaction of NaNHPh with (Me2SiO)n / hexamethylcyclotrisiloxane.",
        "reagents": [
          {
            "name": "gadolinium(III) bromide",
