        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "General procedure for 6–8 under N2: suspend ca. 2 g LnCl3 or SmBr3 in 25 mL THF and add dropwise at 0 °C a solution of three equivalents of LiNHtBu in ca. 35 mL THF, sealing joints with Baysilone grease (source of the oxasilylamido ligand). Warming gives yellow to orange solutions in 5 min; after 3–4 h the solvent is removed in vacuo. The residue is treated with 60 mL toluene, stirred 4 h at 20 °C, filtered from LiCl, concentrated to 15 mL and left at 20 °C for 2 d. Isolated colorless single crystals 2–6%. Specific for 6: 2.64 g SmBr3 (6.7 mmol), 20 mL THF, 1.61 g LiNHtBu (20.3 mmol) in 25 mL THF; 200 mg isolated crystals. Analytical formula of the isolated powder is given as C20H48Li2N3O3Si2Sm (599.02).",
